WEBVTT

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:07.510
<i>The AE Virus, a deadly virus with a fatality 
rate of 100%, has ravaged the Earth.</i>

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:11.140
<i>The crew has come to Mars 
in order to find a vaccine.</i>

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.150
<i>But they found themselves under 
unexpected attack by the terraformars,</i>

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:22.160
<i>and most of their comrades missing.</i>

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:26.290
Right now, all we can do is 
believe that everyone is safe.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.860
You've already sent a 
giant rescue ship, right?

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:36.160
Let's all go back to Earth! Go, go!

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.280
<b><i>The Captain's Rage</i></b>

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.320
We should reach the main ship today.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:33.880
Yeah.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.210
What is it?

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.690
There've been no attacks for the last six days.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.370
Is that all?

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.340
No, I just don't want to believe it.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:52.100
What Adolf said about 
No. 4 Division being wiped out.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.670
They had a lot of engineers there.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.570
Even their leader was only Mars Ranking 44.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.980
<b>Mars Ranking: A numerical indicator 
of one's ability to defeat terraformars.</b>

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.570
Yeah.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.660
The day I told all the higher-ranking 
crew that I would be the captain...

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.190
Food?

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.290
I don't mind.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.020
Sounds great.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.750
Take me someplace with good alcohol.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.830
Your first choice is always alcohol, huh?

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.350
That's the Japanese for you.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.720
You plan on using alcohol 
to win over your men?

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.170
<b>Scum...</b>

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.060
To be honest, I'd rather not.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.930
But you'll just tell me this 
is part of the job, won't you?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.030
Oh, no...

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.070
Captain!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.990
I want to eat some ramen!

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:38.430
Something so greasy it violates 
every Asian standard of decency.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.370
<i>Liu the Anaconda...</i>

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.910
<i>His cheerful little suggestion was enough 
to make all you stubborn weirdos...</i>

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.810
Glad I came!

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:55.040
This is the kind of tradition-wrecking 
deliciousness that I was hoping for.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.560
Now that we've had our fill,

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.880
ready to go drink?

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.840
That's a great idea, Liu-san.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.910
...come together more.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.460
<i>It helped me out a lot.</i>

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.660
What the hell are you doing?

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.880
Morning calisthenics.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.780
Just like he does.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.060
He never changes.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.580
<b>5 Days Ago
 U-NASA Emergency Leaders Briefing</b>

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.790
We've sent no rescue ship for Plan Delta.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.480
<b>U-NASA 6th Branch Office
Roman Commonwealth President
 Luke Snorresson</b>

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.550
What did you say?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.880
The rescue ship we were planning on 
sending has encountered continued

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.860
<b>U-NASA 1st Branch Office
US President Gerald Goodman</b>

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.890
problems and we don't know 
when we'll be able to launch.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.100
<b>U-NASA 2nd Branch Office
Japanese Prime Minister Hiruma Ichiro</b>

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.360
<i>Like hell it has.</i>

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.500
<i>You guys are the world's 
leaders in space development.</i>

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.690
<i>If it's true, that means 
that some other country—</i>

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.060
Which means...

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:03.530
It all comes down to whether the 
crashed Annex 1 can be repaired.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.370
<b>U-NASA 4th Branch Office
Head</b>

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.190
Yes.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.340
<i>This was expected.</i>

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.520
<i>If they can send help, they can get 
a leg up on the other countries...</i>

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:11.490
It was always...

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.710
...a rash plan.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.100
<b>U-NASA 5th Branch Office
German Prime Minister Petra Eheim</b>

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:20.330
We sent our best men and our 
kids with the brightest futures

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:23.700
to a planet with who knows how 
many millions of terraformars,

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.880
and no real weaponry.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.600
The result has been several crew fatalities.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:32.830
<b>U-NASA 3rd Branch Office
Russian Commonwealth President Smiles</b>

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.690
It's true that the risk of having 
any weapons stolen is great,

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:39.290
but there were many ways to deal 
with this, like voice recognition.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.600
In other words, that talk 
of risk was just an excuse.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.830
We could've sent an army armed 
with our latest weapons,

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.800
but we deliberately chose not to.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:54.880
The whole point of this was to do human 
experiments for the M.O. Operations.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.610
<b>Mosaic Organ                                    Human                                Operation Base</b>

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:03.460
<i>He just denied the whole 
point of the Annex Project!</i>

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.170
<i>You're not supposed to say that!</i>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:10.570
We'll take the lead in rescuing 
the people trapped on Mars.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:15.640
We've already sent a rescue ship 
armed with tactical weapons.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:21.440
<i>I can't tell him that he's 
not supposed to have weapons.</i>

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:26.050
<i>His country's military strength 
is overwhelming right now.</i>

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:32.660
<i>If I just spoke the truth, and told him that 
this whole thing was the result of his sabotage,</i>

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.360
<i>we'd have a nuclear war 
on our hands immediately.</i>

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.800
<i>But what's he after?</i>

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:41.100
<i>He can't be interested in taking 
the lead on the project anymore.</i>

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.480
Is he still going?

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.050
That's probably not enough for him.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.050
This is still light for you, isn't it?

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:03.980
No, it's really heavy.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.130
How rude. Add another twenty.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.040
<i>You've really changed, Michelle.</i>

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:15.080
<i>The first time I met you, you were cold 
and shut off from everyone around you.</i>

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:18.810
My life revolves around killing 
as many of them as possible.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.040
I've got no time for anything else.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.030
<i>Your father was a man I 
admired, Donatello K. Davis.</i>

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:31.200
<i>He underwent the Bugs Operation and 
gained the power of the Paraponera.</i>

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:35.380
<i>And you became the first member of humanity 
to genetically inherit their abilities,</i>

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.510
<b>Bullet Ant</b>

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:39.960
<i>which made you all alone in the world.</i>

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:42.270
<i>Akari was the same.</i>

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.350
<i>He became the second post-surgery human,</i>

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:48.780
<i>and was born with the ability to transform, 
which made his life a lonely battle.</i>

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:54.750
<i>Maybe that's why you two 
can understand each other.</i>

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.660
<i>Once this mission is over,</i>

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.330
<i>I hope you live peaceful lives on Earth.</i>

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:03.910
It's so quiet.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.560
It's hard to believe that on 
the first day we had two SOSs.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:08.540
Two?

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:10.850
It wasn't just the one from No. 6 Division?

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.300
What are you talking about?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.260
Your No. 1 Division sent 
the first one, right?

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.000
We managed to rendezvous, so I 
didn't mention it in my report.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:17.920
Wait a second.

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:21.760
We didn't send any SOS.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:22.770
What?

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.070
What do you think?

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.470
<b>Russia & Northern Europe No. 3 Division</b>

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.490
Wow.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:31.820
It's nothing like the storeroom 
we saw on the first day.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.190
Who would believe there're domes 
like this under the pyramids?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.570
Was this made by Rahab, the god of Mars?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.520
Nope, it wasn't.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:41.740
<b>Team 3 Chief
 Sylvester Asimov</b>

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.340
They remade this,

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.740
centered around a single leader.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.310
According to the reports twenty years ago,

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:55.180
there was a terraformar who possessed 
a high level of intelligence.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.350
It would use what looked like martial arts,

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.810
take actions to command its companions,

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:06.600
and showed interest in the bodies of 
those who'd undergone the Bugs Operation.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.870
And now we find this ridiculous room.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.380
One of them was smart enough 
to look at the stars

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.890
and understand that Mars was a sphere,

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.270
and even successfully 
complete a Bugs Operation.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.360
He was a general with a 
clear vision, a sharp mind,

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:30.370
and a high level of charisma.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.590
But he's dead.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:36.680
That's why no one has followed us this far.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.640
Chief.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:38.340
What is it?

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.970
I found something you're 
not going to believe.

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:59.390
Not bad, you little bastards.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:05.150
That makes me worry about what Adolf said.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.420
The burnt bodies of all of No. 4 division.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.300
Yes.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:12.740
The terraformars are 
interested in our bodies.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.770
They wouldn't burn them to a crisp 
and leave them on the ground.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:17.840
Which means that was...

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.760
An attempt to hide who those bodies were.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.470
So that even if they're out of 
contact, no one will suspect them,

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.230
and they can act in secret.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:27.350
The whole Earth may be working 
together on this mission,

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.730
but in the end, it's still just 
a bunch of different countries.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.840
I don't want to believe it, but...

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:33.770
There was a traitor!

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.910
Mines, okay!

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.960
<b>The mothership of the Annex Project. 
On March 4th, 2620 it left Earth with 100 members
of the U-NASA Mars Search Team.
It arrived 38 days later.
It was equipped with an artificial low-gravity area
for the living quarters, as well as facilities to allow 
research on the AE virus, 
which was the primary goal
of the mission</b>

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.960
<b>Large Manned Spacecraft "Annex 1"</b>

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.780
So, as you can see...

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.640
In addition to the use of nets,

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:06.580
<b>Bao Zhilan, China
 Mars Ranking 50</b>

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.180
if you'd like to take them alive destroying

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.590
their arms and legs is also an 
extremely effective measure.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:11.890
<b>Jet, Thailand
 Mars Ranking 61</b>

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:14.260
I'm sure you wouldn't want 
to do this to a human being,

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:18.190
but unlike us, those two were born insects.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.770
<b>Xi Chun-Li, China 
Mars Ranking 99</b>

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:21.160
Just think of them as terraformars.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.100
<b>Borgijin Dorjiberke, Mongolia
 Mars Ranking 49</b>

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:22.360
Ow!

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:30.540
We would like to take the 
two samples alive, but...

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:34.910
<b>Liu Yiwu, China
 Mars Ranking 44</b>

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.510
if they have to die, 
their bodies will serve, too.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:40.110
So, the targets will 
probably be arriving today.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.320
<b>China & Asia No. 4 Division</b>

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:44.010
Ideally they'll injure themselves 
on the minefield, but...

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:46.970
What's that sound?

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:02.370
I won't get mad, so whoever forgot to 
raise the AA Shield, raise your hand.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.530
I knew it was you, Hong-chan.

00:12:05.770 --> 00:12:08.290
I-I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.510
That's strange.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:12.110
<b>Hong, China
 Mars Ranking 97</b>

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:13.540
There was a circle and a 
line, and I hit the circle.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.540
<b>I think I got it right?</b>

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.100
It's the opposite, fool!

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.320
I told you that's a zero and a one!

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.510
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:12:19.810 --> 00:12:21.270
Well, whatever.

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:24.250
This is the perfect time for some 
multi-target combat training.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:25.720
Jet!

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:27.210
Right here.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.410
Okay!

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.380
Everyone, attention!

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:57.740
So they're just flying right into it?

00:12:57.740 --> 00:13:00.210
Their attack patterns are much 
simpler than the first day.

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:05.840
Now, will they realize that the 
weapon targets you if you move?

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:15.400
Th-The tools of civilization are amazing!

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.740
Captain, what's that?

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:33.040
What's that doing here?

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.120
Unit 2, halt!

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.470
What's wrong, Captain?

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:48.140
There's a radio tower.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.220
Looks like we were right.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:55.290
There are people in front of Annex 1.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.050
There's something surrounding them...

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.010
...in a wide area.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.610
It's probably mines.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.850
That's No. 4 Division!

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:05.580
What?

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:06.740
A-Are they ghosts?

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.250
Erika, get me in touch with Earth.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:09.990
Hurry!

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:10.950
Right!

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.650
You've made me sad, Liu-san.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.340
If you're going to hit me this hard...

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:25.510
...I've got to hit back!

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:30.840
So he did notice?

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:34.330
I liked you, Captain.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:36.680
And I owe you for the drinks.

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:40.850
But the nine billion people on Earth

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.610
can't be like the hundred 
people on Annex 1 anymore.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:47.790
Everyone, prepare for combat!

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.910
<i>This message is from the US and Japanese 
No. 1 and No. 2 divisions from Annex 1.</i>

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.630
What's going on?

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:13.060
The message cut off!

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:14.560
What about the spare communication lines?

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:16.380
No good.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:17.770
The signal's cut off.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.330
Captain! Captain!

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.770
We can't communicate at all.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:23.810
What?

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:28.050
The device itself is working properly, but...

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:29.780
No way...

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:31.650
Aah, aah.

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.090
<i>Test, test! Do you read,</i>

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.930
<i>Joint US-Japanese division?</i>

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:37.830
<i>This is the chief of No. 4 Division, Liu.</i>

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:43.750
You brought a whole pile of corpses 
to hide what you were up to.

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:45.340
That's right.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.460
Were you the ones who cut the

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:51.050
security cameras so they could sneak 
onboard just before we landed?

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:52.760
Yes.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.810
You bought off the leaders to 
make them cancel the return

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.830
to Earth and initiate plan Delta, didn't you?

00:15:58.830 --> 00:15:59.850
That's right!

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:04.260
Do you know how many people you killed?

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:05.550
What are you planning?

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:08.390
I'm done, Executive Officer Davis.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:12.030
All we're interested in 
is what's below your neck.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:17.490
<i>No. 4 Division has taken complete 
control of all communications.</i>

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.580
<i>Crying to Earth won't help you.</i>

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.380
<i>So, let's get to the point.</i>

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:28.200
<i>I'm thinking about shooting 
some missiles at you.</i>

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.800
<i>Two, to be precise. The best we've got.</i>

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:34.790
They're very, very expensive, 
so they don't miss.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.030
There's a 200% chance you won't survive.

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:38.630
If you don't want that,

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:43.290
<i>have Hizamaru-kun and Davis-san 
run towards us, unarmed.</i>

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:49.760
Wait!

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:54.160
I understand that you chose 
your comrade's safety

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.850
over your own, without a moment's hesitation.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:58.280
But calm down.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:00.170
That's right, Akari.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:03.300
If you care about us, 
you should do the opposite.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:09.210
After they've got you and the XO, 
they're going to kill us, 100%.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.530
Who? What?

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.510
They're shooting a missile?

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.880
Everyone, move over there.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.800
They seem like they're panicking.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.420
I guess it's natural.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:24.850
Yup. You're locked on, right?

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:26.990
Yes.

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:31.760
If they start running in groups, 
or try to back off, fire.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.110
General Liu, they're back.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:44.950
Not bad.

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:46.040
So what?

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:48.500
The line. The line.

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:49.710
Line!

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:06.480
Don't interfere when we humans are making 
a gentlemanly offer of surrender!

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:12.570
An AA shield!

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.730
They brought something like that, too?

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:16.400
Captain.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.570
Okay...

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:27.930
Don't die!

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:29.840
And complete the mission!

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:32.090
I'm counting on you guys!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:36.610
Um, Dor-san,

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:41.560
there's no way one of those is going 
to slip through the shields, is there?

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:43.780
Not a chance in a million.

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:48.920
Don't get cocky just because we 
haven't had any weapons so far.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:52.590
Those big, fragile pebbles 
aren't going to hit us.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:53.610
Fools!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.990
If you want to hit us that badly,

00:18:55.990 --> 00:19:00.410
bring a rifle with a scope, computer, 
and stealth capabilities!

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:15.440
That's right.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:17.460
They had someone who could 
throw rocks as fast as bullets,

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.510
and a bird-woman that's 
as fast as a jet fighter!

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:22.990
Just like the sign.

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:25.650
Like throwing through the eye of a needle.

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:26.640
Go play in the Majors.

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:27.270
Sure thing.

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:31.020
Hey, did that shock wave kill anybody?

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.330
We're fine.

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:41.880
Your traitorous acts have exposed the 
rest of the crew to mortal danger.

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:45.450
Division Chief, Liu Yiwu, 
and the remaining sixteen of you...

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:47.910
Feel free to keep your weapons.

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.430
But line up!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.490
You monsters...

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.910
You really think we're just going to line up?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:59.520
We're traitors, and we have you surrounded.

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:08.540
Well done, Jet-kun.

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:11.560
Everyone, keep your distance, and fire!

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:12.730
Li!

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:21.070
That last one wasn't luck?

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:23.530
Mars Ranking 12...

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:25.230
<b>Mars Ranking 12
Alex Kandori Stewart
US-Japanese Joint No. 2 Division
Operation Base - Harpy Eagle</b>

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.280
What amazing control!

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:26.610
You missed.

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.670
Li, cut the magnet now!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.280
Voice recognition! Jet!

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.630
<i>That's why I hate voice recognition!</i>

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:46.560
I don't want to fight you.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:50.240
Let me negotiate with the First.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:52.810
Don't call her that.

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:55.690
Her name is Michelle K. Davis.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:58.600
Acting Captain Michelle K. Davis.

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:02.740
The woman who carries the blood 
of the warrior I respect the most.

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:06.450
Michelle has grown up into a splendid woman.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:10.660
She's become a person who can lead 
herself and the people around her.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:14.480
She's not a sample for you to play with!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.030
I understand how you feel.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:19.670
But she's just a valuable sample.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.600
<i>We'll both hit at the same time.</i>

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.650
<i>But he's an amateur, not a soldier!</i>

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.610
<i>He'll be just a second slow!</i>

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:05.370
<i>It's over, Liu.</i>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>An Alliance Appears</b>

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:40.230
Give the traitors Sign A!
